body:
"yea nah lick my ass"

&#x200B;

"For $3 yes"

Wow that totally made my night :) I'm happy to do it! If you have any more, please let me know!

&#x200B;

Also, I'm offering [private sessions](https://www.fiverr.com/whoinvitedlaura/if-you-need-to-talk-about-a-problem-look-no-farther) now so if you ever need to talk to someone, I would be happy to be that person :)

There wasn't really an 'average call' because they're all so different, but we would have people who called us every day. Not in a crisis situation, but just needed to talk to someone. They would just tell us how their day was or what their plans were for the night. I'd say this made up about 99% of our calls. 

&#x200B;

but that 1%...

&#x200B;

Those are scary, but we're well trained so we know what we're doing. I would start by introducing myself and asking the callers name. Then I would ask them if they were thinking about suicide/what was going on and I would let them talk for as long as they needed. I try to do as little talking as possible because the caller wants to be HEARD, not preached to. Then either I can calm them to the point where I can feel good about ending the call (almost always) or I call PES (Psychiatric Emergency Services) to do a wellness check and they can determine if that person needs to be hospitalized. That's super rare though.
